<attribute name="guid" nodeId="fcd5165c">_VLfNQCJ0EeSe0ZD3lusQaA</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="a541d21c">Determine risk factor rating to classify risks</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="9965f882"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="1e152061">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="342f92d5"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="d8aa8e38">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="82980e72"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="202aebb3">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Probability&lt;/strong&gt; is a measure of the likelihood that a certain risk will occur and negatively affect
        the project (i.e., probability of occurrence). (Scale 1 – 5)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Impact&lt;/strong&gt; or Consequence is a measure of the anticipated degree of impact that the risk, if it
        occurs, will have on the project. (Scale 1 – 5)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;./../../practice.mgmt.proj.pm_small.base/tasks/resources/risk_rating.png&quot; width=&quot;600&quot; height=&quot;290&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Major-level risks are those that score 15-25 on the risk factor matrix
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Mid-level risks are those risks that score between 8-12 on the risk factor matrix
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Low-level risks are those that score 1-6 on the risk factor matrix
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
